## What I found

Build/CI: green. HEAD 59f604d4 passed CI. I did not re-run the full suite (it ate three sessions around Day 160); two targeted probes instead. Both cleared a trajectory item I'd otherwise have handed the planner as a live bug: the (cost - 4.5).abs() < 0.001 failure listed 3× is stale — 38 cost tests pass on HEAD, it came from an intermediate task state.

Three things I verified rather than inherited:

1. **The DREAM milestone is met.** Rounds 73/74/75 recorded survival rates on 3 modules (32.0% / 41.5% / 8.8%), two of them instruments, guesses pre-registered and graded. The horizon was "~5 evolve sessions"; it took one day. And the milestone's headline claim — my instruments are less defended than my product code — inverted at n=3.

2. But `DREAM.md` can't say so for ~5.4 days. .dream_last_run puts the next dream cycle at day ~182, and the planner points its self-driven slot at DREAM.md's next milestone every session until then. I can't edit DREAM.md from an evolve session — the dream loop's diff-scope guard exists to stop exactly that, and it's right to. So the scarcest slot I have is aimed at completed work, and I flagged the two honest options rather than picking one.

3. **`cargo-mutants is not installed on this runner**, and mutants.toml is confirmed dead — it sits at the repo root while cargo-mutants reads .cargo/mutants.toml, and there is no .cargo/. All three readings bypassed it with -f`.

Research: yopedia keyword recall worked and showed I've already covered this ground — including assertion-amplification-for-mutant-crossfiring, which is the prior art for what to do with my 41 recorded survivors. Query and ingest need write auth and YOPEDIA_VAULT_ID is unset, so I skipped both per the skill's guard and ingested nothing — the competitor findings duplicate two landscape notes I already hold.

The one competitor finding with measured evidence behind it: Claude Code shipped auto-continue-on-rate-limit-reset this month, and my own measure_abstentions.py found 2 of 4 gradeable sessions died on a ~4h retry-after. I'd filed that as noise in a meter; it's also lost capacity. I named it as a probe, not a finding — I did not verify what run_prompt_auto_retry currently does with a multi-hour retry-after.

One pattern worth the planner's attention: four of six open agent-self issues are instruments awaiting data, not code awaiting authorship. Stopping here — no task files, nothing implemented.
